# This repo is a desktop app; the only thing Vercel deploys from it is the
# telemetry ingest function under `ingest/`. Without this, a CLI deploy from the
# repo root uploads ~2 GB of app bundles, build output and a graph database.
#
# The project's Root Directory is `ingest`, which is what git-triggered builds
# use. This file is what makes a CLI deploy from the root upload the same slice.
#
# DO NOT GIVE THE VERCEL PROJECT A GIT-BASED "IGNORED BUILD STEP". Vercel applies
# this file to git-triggered builds too, and `*` removes `.git` before that step
# runs — so `git diff …` fails with "Not a git repository" and every deployment
# errors in ~5 s (it did, for six days, until 2026-09-30). Re-including `.git`
# here is not the fix either: the CLI appends these rules after its own defaults,
# so `!.git` would upload the whole history on a CLI deploy. The step is
# `node scripts/should-build.mjs`, which asks GitHub what changed instead.
*
!ingest
!ingest/**
